Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:58:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: tab shape with smaller top
 radius, straight base

From Titin's design (softmac FlyWeb/branding/interfaz-3.2.0):
- Top corner radius 3 dip instead of Chromium's 10, estimated from the
  mockup in proportion to the tab height (BRAVE_TAB_STYLE_TOP_CORNER_RADIUS
  in chromium_src/chrome/browser/ui/tabs/tab_style.cc).
- Straight join with the toolbar: the outward curves at the base are not
  drawn (kFlyWebTabBottomCornerRadius = 0 in the chromium_src override of
  horizontal_tab_style_views.cc).

TabStyle::GetBottomCornerRadius() is unchanged because it also sets the
tab width and the overlap between tabs, so the tab size stays as it is.
Inactive tabs keep no background and the separators between them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2juPkbC58kEi4QFeyU
